From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: keep interrupts disabled in the MMU miss handlers

reload_DMMU_tlb and reload_IMMU_tlb enabled interrupts around the call
of their C handler ("for window spill/fill traps"). They run at TL 1,
where an interrupt goes to the TL>0 trap table, and its level 14 entry
only retries without clearing the interrupt. A timer interrupt pending
when the handler enables interrupts therefore traps again on the same
instruction for good: the CPU spins on the call and nothing else runs.

FreeBSD 12.4 on sun4u hits it on every power-off: shutdown -p now ends
in the "SUNW,power-off" client call with the kernel's %tick compare
interrupt pending (the client interface runs with interrupts disabled,
patch 0016), the firmware takes a DTLB miss in get_property() on the
way to the power register, and the machine stays on after "Uptime:",
QEMU at 100% of a host core (-d int: interrupt 0x4e at that one PC, over
and over). 0030 met the same spin after a reboot and avoided it there by
keeping the firmware's own timer from firing.

Leave interrupts disabled, as the trap left them. Window spill and fill
traps are not interrupts and are taken whatever PSTATE.IE says, and a
pending interrupt is taken when the retry gets back to the code that
missed (the client, or the firmware at TL 0) with its own PSTATE.IE.
---
 arch/sparc64/vectors.S | 34 ++++++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/vectors.S b/arch/sparc64/vectors.S
index 3d6b066..79f1b28 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/vectors.S
+++ b/arch/sparc64/vectors.S
@@ -386,18 +386,15 @@ reload_DMMU_tlb:
 	add	%g1, %g7, %g7
 	mov	%g7, %sp
 
-	/* Enable interrupts for window spill/fill traps */
-	rdpr	%pstate, %g7
-	or	%g7, PSTATE_IE, %g7
-	wrpr	%g7, %pstate	
-
+	/*
+	 * Interrupts stay disabled, as the trap left them: window spill and
+	 * fill traps don't need them, and an interrupt taken here at TL 1
+	 * goes to the TL>0 table, whose level 14 entry only retries. A timer
+	 * interrupt the client left pending (FreeBSD's, when it calls in to
+	 * power off) then kept the CPU on this call for good.
+	 */
 	call	dtlb_miss_handler
 	 nop
-
-	/* Disable interrupts */
-	rdpr	%pstate, %g7
-	andn	%g7, PSTATE_IE, %g7
-	wrpr	%g7, %pstate
 	
 	/* Restore CPU state from stack */
 	setx	_fcstack_ptr, %g6, %g7
@@ -472,18 +469,15 @@ reload_IMMU_tlb:
 	add	%g1, %g7, %g7
 	mov	%g7, %sp
 
-	/* Enable interrupts for window spill/fill traps */
-	rdpr	%pstate, %g7
-	or	%g7, PSTATE_IE, %g7
-	wrpr	%g7, %pstate	
-
+	/*
+	 * Interrupts stay disabled, as the trap left them: window spill and
+	 * fill traps don't need them, and an interrupt taken here at TL 1
+	 * goes to the TL>0 table, whose level 14 entry only retries. A timer
+	 * interrupt the client left pending (FreeBSD's, when it calls in to
+	 * power off) then kept the CPU on this call for good.
+	 */
 	call	itlb_miss_handler
 	 nop
-
-	/* Disable interrupts */
-	rdpr	%pstate, %g7
-	andn	%g7, PSTATE_IE, %g7
-	wrpr	%g7, %pstate
 	
 	/* Restore CPU state from stack */
 	setx	_fcstack_ptr, %g6, %g7
